  "summary_en": "Creates points that represent implicit surfaces, which add collision objects to a Pyro simulation. Mainly for basic primitives (box, sphere, torus, tube), and can also take a more complex implicit surface as its collision shape. Output is source_points, the points carrying Pyro collision attributes.",
  "inputs": [
    "implicitsurface (optional): implicit surface built with the SOP-based implicit surface workflow"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Activation: 1 turns the node on, 0 turns it off",
    "Shape: selects the primitive, which determines the other controls",
    "Shape Box: Size (with per-component option), Roundness (0 gives sharp edges)",
    "Shape Sphere: Radius (with per-component option), Radius Scale, Cut Sphere with a Y-position plane",
    "Shape Torus: major and tube radius, Link Length (0 gives a regular torus)",
    "Shape Tube: Length, end Radius values (matching values give a straight tube), Radius Scale, Round Caps",
    "Transform: Translate, Rotate X Y Z, Uniform Scale",
    "Collision: Collision Velocity (motion-based velocity estimate for moving or rotating sources), Velocity Scale"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Requires DOP-level permissions; not in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education",
    "Connect the output to the collision_points input of a Pyro Block Begin node",
    "For multiple collisions, merge several outputs with a Point Merge node",
    "The page does not describe the similarly named Pyro Collision from Shape node, which is only linked under See also"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Pyro Collision Shape crée des points représentant des surfaces implicites (boîte, sphère, tore, tube) qui servent d'obstacles à une simulation Pyro."
